What is Module?
-In Python Programming, a module is a file that contains 
 Python code (functions, variables, classes, etc.)
-Any file which ends with .py extension is called as module.

What is Package?
- Collection of related modules is called as package.

__init__ (Define its a package)
-------------------------------
-Every Package should contains _ _init_ _.py file then only your python treat
 that it is package up to Python <3.3, But later versions It’s Optional.

import keyword
---------------
-If you want to use one module to another module the use 'import' keyword.
-Syntax: import modulename
-Because of import keyword all the members of your module is loaded in your 
 program .
-Now if you want to access data then ->Modulename.variablename
                                     ->Modulename.functionname()
-If you want to import a module from another location then we need to use complete path.
-We can set alias name to your path so we can access your variable and functions by using alias names.
  -eg- import Amazon.Product.items  -This is called absulute path
       import Amazon.Product.items as ai -Alias name

